    <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>The county did not adopt a moratorium of its own — it passed a resolution affirming local zoning authority and urging its municipalities to consider one. Tracked as a signal, not a restriction</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Mohawk (Montgomery Co.): data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/mohawk-montgomery-co-ny</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-mohawk-(montgomery-co.)-ny</guid>
    <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>6-month pause to write zoning rules; public hearing Aug 13, 2026. Supervisor cites the state EO&#x27;s 50 MW floor as leaving smaller facilities unregulated. Would run to Feb 13, 2027 if adopted</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>New York (statewide): data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/new-york-statewide-ny</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-new-york-(statewide)-ny</guid>
    <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>EO 62: first statewide pause. Holds DEC discretionary approvals for 50+ MW facilities until DPS finishes a generic environmental impact statement — roughly a year, but tied to that study, not a fixed date</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>New York (S10642/A11560): data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/new-york-s10642-a11560-ny</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-new-york-(s10642/a11560)-ny</guid>
    <pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Responsible Data Center Development Act: 1-year moratorium on state permits for 20+ MW facilities, plus a dedicated utility rate class, a DEC impact study, and a host-community benefit program. Passed the Senate 43-17. Per the Senate&#x27;s own record it had not been delivered to the Governor as of Aug 4, 2026 — Hochul acted by executive order (EO 62, 50 MW floor) instead. Still live, and stricter than the EO</description>
  </item>
